  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">The 1928 Book of Common Prayer is the last revision of the American Prayer Book before the controversial 1979 edition that replaced it. Its Morning Prayer and Evening Prayer preserve the structure Cranmer laid down in 1549: opening sentences, confession, absolution, psalms, lessons, canticles, creed, suffrages, collects, and closing prayers. The daily office is the heartbeat of Anglican devotion, meant to be prayed morning and evening without fail. This edition presents the original Elizabethan English alongside a modernized reading for those who prefer contemporary language, while preserving the cadence and theology of the text.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
